From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Ludovic Henry <git@ludovic.dev>
Date: Fri, 23 Oct 2026 23:50:00 +0000
Subject: [PATCH] setup: take the wheel version from PNNX_VERSION

setup.py stamps the wheel with the build date (time.strftime("%Y%m%d")),
which is how upstream versions each release: the release workflow builds
on the day it publishes. This port rebuilds an already-released version
from the commit it was cut from, so the build date is the wrong version:
CI run 38676705597 built pnnx-20261015 wheels for the 20260526 release,
and jobs straddling midnight UTC would produce mixed versions that the
publish step rejects. Let the workflow pass the release's version in
PNNX_VERSION, falling back to the build date when it is unset.

Upstream-Status: Inappropriate [riscv64 port rebuilds a past date-stamped release; upstream versions wheels by their build date]
---
 tools/pnnx/python/setup.py | 2 +-
 1 file changed, 1 insertion(+), 1 deletion(-)

diff --git a/tools/pnnx/python/setup.py b/tools/pnnx/python/setup.py
index bb3ca546..73560f8a 100644
--- a/tools/pnnx/python/setup.py
+++ b/tools/pnnx/python/setup.py
@@ -10,7 +10,7 @@ from setuptools.command.build_ext import build_ext
 from setuptools.command.install import install

 def set_version():
-    pnnx_version = time.strftime("%Y%m%d", time.localtime())
+    pnnx_version = os.environ.get("PNNX_VERSION") or time.strftime("%Y%m%d", time.localtime())
     return pnnx_version

 # Parse environment variables
